Archie: navigation buttons and a search box in the sidebar.

  - Back, Forward and Reload buttons sit at the bottom of the vertical tab
    strip, next to the new tab button. Back/Forward/Reload dim when they
    can't be used.
  - The sidebar's new tab button opens a floating search box
    (ArchieCommandBar) instead of a blank tab. Enter opens what you typed
    in a new tab: an address is opened directly, anything else is searched
    with the default search engine, using the omnibox's own classifier.
    Esc or clicking elsewhere closes it without opening a tab.
    Middle-click (paste and go) and the button's context menu still work.

